- Find if the universal proposer can be improved such that it can suggest and set generations and population according to formula difficulty and if possible other parameters too.
- Add a Heterogeneous First Layer (EQL Layer): Before the GLU layers in the curve classifier, add a parallel linear layer with explicit mathematical activations (e.g., sin, cos, exp, log) so the network can "test" transformations on raw curve features.
- PointNet / CNN Tokenization for Raw Curves: Introduce a 1D Conv layer over the raw signal to extract a sequence of "shape patches" prior to the attention mechanism, replacing the single-token representation for raw features.
- Shift to Seq2Seq Architecture (Long Term): Transition from multi-label classification to an Auto-Regressive Decoder that directly predicts the abstract syntax tree (AST) of mathematical operators in Reverse Polish Notation.

- modularize the benchmark code so multiple benchmark scripts like benchmark_suite.py and run_srbench_local.py can share the same codebase for evaluation, data loading, and model inference. This will allow us to easily test new models across different benchmarks without duplicating code and also make it easier to maintain and update the evaluation logic in one place.  